  "decisions": [
    "No capture engine, channels, driver, dependency, wireless restore, resource thresholds, UI or timer changes.",
    "Use existing background resource probe; add bounded proc reads, no extra timer or polling thread.",
    "After authenticated host-key identity binding: read health once; after unexpected disconnect read fault logs on same-device reconnect. Regular-capture failure also reads fault logs while still connected.",
    "Boot ID changed means another kernel boot. Same boot ID means same kernel boot, not proof of driver health. Uptime decrease without boot ID is supporting evidence only.",
    "Missing proc fields, logread, dmesg or pstore stay unknown; no installs or mount operations.",
    "Sources present only records command/path presence, not proof that the log is readable. Completed means collection protocol completed, not a diagnosis or proof of no fault.",
    "pstore reads at most two existing ramoops files with 4096 bytes per file; never clears kernel logs or removes crash records.",
    "Samples and incidents are bounded and exported through the existing masked ZIP journal.",
    "History compares within the running application session. Application restart loses the in-memory baseline; existing exported contexts remain evidence.",
    "Architecture/model-independent proc ABI; no radio, chipset, package manager or target-specific dispatch. No claim of per-model live acceptance.",
    "Regular capture: sample before hcxdumptool/airodump-ng process starts; piggyback proc reads on existing read-only PID verification commands. No new recheck interval or supervisor traffic.",
    "The PID-check shell wrapper preserves original exit codes, including resource exits 80/81, and strips diagnostic output before returning to the original caller.",
    "Regular capture common failure finalization also collects filtered kernel/system/pstore evidence while connected; disconnected collection stays local and the next same-device login gathers post-loss evidence."
  ],
